 InfiniSplat v2 is a feed-forward Gaussian reconstruction method for arbitrary input views that decouples geometry and attribute prediction, uses ground-truth (GT) camera poses for alignment during training, and employs large-angle target view supervision to improve rendering quality under large viewpoint changes. It differs from its siblings by freezing the geometry branch to prevent geometric degradation caused by joint optimization, and by using GT poses for alignment to avoid pose errors that misguide the network under large-angle supervision.
 
+### [CodecSplat](18143-codecsplat.md)
+CodecSplat is a compression framework for feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting (FF3DGS) that encodes an intermediate 2D Gaussian-generation feature into an entropy-coded scene bitstream, avoiding the inefficient compression of irregular 3D Gaussian primitives. Unlike existing 3DGS compression methods that compress Gaussian primitives after a structured-to-irregular transformation, CodecSplat places the coding bottleneck before 2D-to-3D Gaussian construction, allowing compression to exploit the structured intermediate feature representation.
